{"content_hash": "sha256:9cedb1a9746637e57cd67638f4242ee914232919c78350c9f2a34184d9a84ee7", "id": "claim:1307.7171v1:pure-stabilizer-clifford-orbit", "kind": "definition", "origin": "SOURCE_OCCURRENCE", "paper_id": "arxiv:1307.7171v1", "produced_at": "2026-08-22T00:00:00Z", "record_revision": 1, "schema": "agtxiv.scientific-claim/1.0.0", "source_anchors": ["anchor:1307.7171v1:stabilizer-free-set"], "supersedes": null, "text": "For a prime dimension d, the pure stabilizer states are the orbit of the computational-basis state |0> under the Clifford group C_d. The source writes this set as {S_i} = {U|0> : U in C_d}."}
{"content_hash": "sha256:0f9fee69d2a36254e5fd447b40843abf2d334a5c144985f56f9c5cbd4db37f01", "id": "claim:1307.7171v1:stabilizer-convex-hull", "kind": "definition", "origin": "SOURCE_OCCURRENCE", "paper_id": "arxiv:1307.7171v1", "produced_at": "2026-08-22T00:00:00Z", "record_revision": 1, "schema": "agtxiv.scientific-claim/1.0.0", "source_anchors": ["anchor:1307.7171v1:stabilizer-free-set"], "supersedes": null, "text": "For a prime dimension d, STAB(H_d) is the convex hull of the pure stabilizer states: its elements are density operators sigma expressible as sigma = sum_i p_i S_i for a probability distribution (p_i)."}
{"content_hash": "sha256:14ee4feed9d603964de9937c31b34dbd311ba748eb2a95d993534690d65bd266", "id": "claim:1307.7171v1:magic-membership", "kind": "definition", "origin": "SOURCE_OCCURRENCE", "paper_id": "arxiv:1307.7171v1", "produced_at": "2026-08-22T00:00:00Z", "record_revision": 1, "schema": "agtxiv.scientific-claim/1.0.0", "source_anchors": ["anchor:1307.7171v1:stabilizer-protocol-and-monotone", "anchor:1307.7171v1:resource-split"], "supersedes": null, "text": "A quantum state is magic exactly when it is not a stabilizer state."}
{"content_hash": "sha256:6286ad18ffc3372fff85c46a2fcb0a24e57cd561fb26fa0798618175408136ed", "id": "claim:1307.7171v1:stabilizer-protocol", "kind": "definition", "origin": "SOURCE_OCCURRENCE", "paper_id": "arxiv:1307.7171v1", "produced_at": "2026-08-22T00:00:00Z", "record_revision": 1, "schema": "agtxiv.scientific-claim/1.0.0", "source_anchors": ["anchor:1307.7171v1:stabilizer-operations", "anchor:1307.7171v1:stabilizer-protocol-and-monotone"], "supersedes": null, "text": "A stabilizer protocol is a finite-dimensional state map composed from Clifford unitaries, composition with stabilizer states, computational-basis measurement on the final qudit, partial trace of the final qudit, and conditioning these operations on measurement outcomes or classical randomness."}
{"content_hash": "sha256:6998f906d7a5180e626c9f093d2b49230be518daafea40ae7b7b48a1babf19cf", "id": "claim:1307.7171v1:magic-monotone", "kind": "definition", "origin": "SOURCE_OCCURRENCE", "paper_id": "arxiv:1307.7171v1", "produced_at": "2026-08-22T00:00:00Z", "record_revision": 1, "schema": "agtxiv.scientific-claim/1.0.0", "source_anchors": ["anchor:1307.7171v1:magic-monotone", "anchor:1307.7171v1:stabilizer-protocol-and-monotone"], "supersedes": null, "text": "A magic monotone is a real-valued function on density operators of every finite dimension that does not increase on average under any stabilizer protocol."}
